<title>ITALY: Italy firm has United cargo conversion deal.</title>
<headline>Italy firm has United cargo conversion deal.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Officine Aereonavali Venezia, a unit of Italy's biggest defence and aerospace group Finmeccanica, has signed a deal with United Airlines worth some 40 billion lire to convert four DC-10s to cargo from passenger aircraft.</p>
<p>Finmeccanica is controlled by state industrial holding company IRI.</p>
<p>A statement said the first two converted planes were due to be delivered by next March and the other two by September 1997.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
